From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:28:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: mask fused-MoE K loads on Triton 3.2

Triton 3.2 on MUSA software-pipelines the fused-MoE K loop and issues the
loads of the following K tiles without a bound. When BLOCK_SIZE_K divides
K the kernel loads B, and the K range of A, unmasked, so the prefetch after
the last tile reads past the end of the last expert's weights and faults
when that address is unmapped. Take the K-masked load path on Triton 3.2;
the masked prefetch stays inside both operands.
---
 vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py b/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py
index e0aef0ad89..027e17f106 100644
--- a/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py
@@ -890,7 +890,8 @@ def invoke_fused_moe_triton_kernel(
     BLOCK_SIZE_K = config.pop("BLOCK_SIZE_K")
     if block_shape is not None:
         BLOCK_SIZE_K = min(BLOCK_SIZE_K, min(block_shape[0], block_shape[1]))
-    even_Ks = B.size(2) % BLOCK_SIZE_K == 0
+    # MUSA: Triton 3.2 pipelines unmasked loads past the last K tile.
+    even_Ks = B.size(2) % BLOCK_SIZE_K == 0 and not is_musa_triton_32()
     if use_td and A.size(1) % BLOCK_SIZE_K != 0:
         # TD gather/load feeding tl.dot with a non-block-aligned K
         # miscompiles (~74% of output elements wrong) on real HW;
